Z||000003||batboy||03-24-2001||10:56 PM||||2birds, that's what I was thinking too, but didn't want to sound stupid in case I was wrong. There is a bushing on the passenger side where the inner tie rod goes in. Rodney Dickman has a metal replacement bushing for that, but I sure would not use poly there. Maybe he means the steering column coupler? We need more info!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batkid3.gif">    <B>BATBOY</B><BR>1985 SE auto with 350 Chevy V8 (Batmobile),<BR>suspension mods, lowered, GA brakes, battery<BR>relocated up front, stereo mods, etc...||||reg||1
Z||000004||gixxer||03-25-2001||12:00 AM||||He's talking about the two "D" bushings that attach the rack to the car. Each attach point has two bolts.<BR>A good idea, maybe. It would be easy to return to stock if the steering kickback was too much. <BR>Let us know if you find anything, my rubber jobbies are getting a bit crusty.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||03-25-2001||12:16 AM||||I remember the straps holding it on, but I still don't recall any rubber being in there.  Not like a Mustang where there are two bolts in a bushing that goes through the rack body to bolt it to the car.<P>As far as the steering coupler joint goes, I wonder if a U-joint (like a Borgeson, that the street rodders use) would work, and if it would make any difference||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||03-25-2001||08:42 AM||||if you can find those bushings, let us all know. <P>on the other hand, i really don't see how it will affect handling very much.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||03-25-2001||10:10 AM||||I just double-checked(in shorts and t-shirt in 30 degree weahter, COLD!). It might be different for pre-'88 Fieros, but my ('88)Formula definitely has those "D" shaped steering rack mount bushings. I was thinking about seeing if I could get the dimensions I need and either find some that would work, or see if I could have a set made. My only guess is that steering response might be a little quicker. I've already got poly control arm bushings installed, and love them. Just looking to get the most that I can.||||reg||1
Z||000008||gixxer||03-25-2001||01:03 PM||||I'd be willing to go in with you on a set of custom bushes, as long as the price is reasonable. I have a Formula also, so we're OK there..||||reg||1
